\title{Definition tables: what is being measured}
\description{
A definition is a list of codes with a name. Beyond the name, the coding system and the code, a row may declare the role the event plays, whether the code can diagnose or only date, and the range of dates in which it applies.
}
\details{
Roles are birth, cohort, disease, comorbidity, treatment, marker and mortality. A marker says which population the analysis is about and never starts a follow-up or acts as an outcome. A code whose use is "date" cannot establish the event but can supply its earliest date in a person who has it on other evidence; a definition made only of such codes is refused.
}
